 "description": "Paths the renderer must survive and draw as Chrome does: fills and strokes with finite coordinates as large as 1e30 (bounds past the i32 range, which Skia's safeRoundOut pins to +-(2^31-1)>>2), and dash lists that would cut more than 1,000,000 dashes (SkDashPath gives up and the stroke is drawn undashed: a hairline, a round-capped line, a butt-capped polyline; a butt-capped line has already become a fill of the line, which covers nothing), and dashed strokes of a cubic whose control points are 1e20 or 1e30 (round-capped width 4, and hairlines of width 1 and 0.5), which the dasher also gives up on and draws undashed (the points of those curves are finite, but past the square root of the f32 range, so hairlines are cut into Skia's hairline lines as SkScan_Hairline.cpp does). Each case is clipped to its own 32x64 cell (a translated group clips in its own space)",
